# Which type each field's generated SQL navigates as, and which of the three rungs said so. The
# whole point of the relation is that the answer is often not the type the field's signature names,
# so the example is three fields that disagree with their signatures in three different ways and one
# that does not.

type Film @table(name: "film") { title: String }

# The top rung. @asConnection rewrote this field's type from a list of Film to a synthesised
# connection, so the field's own named type is now the wrapper and the expression the author wrote
# is the only place the element survives. Nothing downstream of capture can recover it.
extend type Query { films: [Film!]! @asConnection }

# The middle rung. The author declared the wrapper rather than asking for one, so no expression
# survives anywhere; what says this field delivers a Film is the structural edges-then-node shape of
# the type it names.
extend type Query { pages: FilmPage }
type FilmPage { edges: [FilmPageEdge!]! pageInfo: PageInfo }
type FilmPageEdge { node: Film cursor: String }
type PageInfo { hasNextPage: Boolean }

# The bottom rung, and the reason the relation is total: a field that returns what it says it
# returns still navigates as something, so a reader joins this relation rather than left-joining it.
extend type Query { firstFilm: Film }

extend schema @assertContains(relation: "graphitron_field_navigation", rows: """
  type_name, field_name, basis,               navigated_type_name
  Query,     films,      CONNECTION_ELEMENT,  Film
  Query,     pages,      CONNECTION_ELEMENT,  Film
  Query,     firstFilm,  NAMED_TYPE,          Film
  Query,     ping,       NAMED_TYPE,          String
  Film,      title,      NAMED_TYPE,          String
  """)

# The wrapper the macro minted is made of fields too, and they navigate on the same rungs as any
# other. Stated because a relation total over the graph's fields includes the generator's own, and a
# reader meeting an unfamiliar type name here should find it accounted for rather than wonder.
extend schema @assertContains(relation: "graphitron_field_navigation", rows: """
  type_name,             field_name, basis,      navigated_type_name
  QueryFilmsConnection,  nodes,      NAMED_TYPE, Film
  QueryFilmsEdge,        node,       NAMED_TYPE, Film
  """)
